# Backend Rules - Metadata-Driven Platform

## Core Technology Stack

- **Framework**: FastAPI 0.104+ with Python 3.11+ for async performance
- **Database**: PostgreSQL 16+ with separate databases per tenant
- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy 2.0+ with async support and metadata-driven models
- **Caching**: Redis 7.2+ for metadata caching and session management
- **Background Jobs**: Celery with Redis broker for workflow automation
- **Validation**: Pydantic v2 for request/response + metadata validation
- **Authentication**: JWT with refresh tokens and 2FA support

## Metadata-First Architecture (MANDATORY)

- **Dynamic APIs**: All CRUD endpoints generated from EntityDefinitions
- **Runtime Validation**: Field validation from FieldDefinitions metadata
- **Workflow Engine**: Trigger-based automation from WorkflowDefinitions
- **Component Catalog**: Serve component metadata to frontend
- **No Hardcoding**: All business logic configurable via metadata

## Architecture Standards

- **Multi-Tenancy**: Separate database per tenant with metadata isolation
- **Async First**: Use async/await for all I/O operations
- **Metadata Engines**: Separate engines for pages, data, UI, workflows, etc.
- **Service Layer**: Business logic separated from API endpoints
- **Repository Pattern**: Data access layer with metadata awareness
- **Event-Driven**: Use events for metadata changes and workflow triggers

## Database Standards (MANDATORY)

- **Metadata Tables**: Core platform tables (entities, fields, layouts, etc.)
- **Tenant Isolation**: Enforce tenant boundaries in all metadata queries
- **Dynamic Models**: Generate SQLAlchemy models from EntityDefinitions
- **Audit Logging**: Track all metadata changes with user attribution
- **Performance**: Proper indexing on metadata queries

- **Runtime Models**: Generate SQLAlchemy models from entity metadata
- **Field Mapping**: Convert field definitions to SQLAlchemy column types
- **Relationship Handling**: Create foreign keys and relationships from metadata

## API Design Standards

- **Metadata APIs**: Dedicated endpoints for serving metadata
- **Dynamic CRUD**: Auto-generated CRUD from EntityDefinitions
- **Component Catalog**: API for component discovery and installation
- **Workflow Engine**: API for trigger management and execution
- **Versioning**: URL-based versioning with metadata compatibility

- **Endpoint Generation**: Create CRUD endpoints from entity definitions
- **Tenant Context**: Always include tenant isolation in API endpoints
- **Metadata Validation**: Validate requests against entity metadata rules

## Metadata Engine Implementation

- **Page Engine**: Serve PageDefinitions with component metadata
- **Data Engine**: Manage EntityDefinitions and FieldDefinitions
- **UI Engine**: Handle LayoutDefinitions and FormDefinitions
- **Workflow Engine**: Process WorkflowDefinitions and triggers
- **Component Engine**: Manage ComponentDefinitions catalog

## Multi-Tenant Database Strategy

- **Master Database**: Global metadata (components, modules, global entities)
- **Tenant Databases**: Tenant-specific data and metadata overrides
- **Connection Routing**: Automatic routing based on tenant context
- **Migration Orchestration**: Parallel migrations across tenant databases
- **Resource Pooling**: Smart pooling based on tenant size

## Error Handling & Logging (MANDATORY)

- **Structured Logging**: JSON-formatted logs with tenant and metadata context
- **Metadata Errors**: Specific error handling for metadata validation
- **Tenant Context**: Always include tenant_id in logs and errors
- **Component Errors**: Handle missing or invalid component definitions
- **Workflow Errors**: Comprehensive workflow execution error handling

## Performance Requirements

- **Metadata Caching**: Redis caching for frequently accessed metadata
- **Dynamic Query Optimization**: Optimize queries based on field definitions
- **Background Processing**: Async workflow execution and metadata updates
- **Connection Pooling**: Per-tenant connection management
- **Response Times**: <200ms for metadata queries, <2s for complex workflows

## Security Implementation (MANDATORY)

- **Metadata Security**: Permission-based access to metadata definitions
- **Component Security**: Validate component access and installation
- **Tenant Isolation**: Strict metadata boundaries between tenants
- **Workflow Security**: Secure workflow execution with permission checks
- **Audit Trail**: Complete logging of metadata changes and access

## Tax Engine Implementation

- **Jurisdiction Management**: Tax rules per country/region
- **Rate Calculations**: Dynamic tax rate application
- **Compliance APIs**: Integration with tax authorities (AADE, etc.)
- **Multi-Currency**: Support for different currencies and rates
- **Audit Requirements**: Tax calculation audit trails

## Billing Engine Implementation

- **Payment Processing**: Multi-provider payment integration
- **Subscription Management**: Usage-based and subscription billing
- **Revenue Recognition**: Proper accounting for platform revenue
- **Marketplace Billing**: Revenue sharing for component creators
- **Compliance**: Financial regulation compliance

## Component & Module System

- **Manifest Processing**: Parse and validate module manifests
- **Dependency Management**: Handle component dependencies
- **Installation**: Secure component installation and updates
- **Marketplace Integration**: Component discovery and purchasing
- **Version Management**: Component versioning and compatibility

## Development Workflow (MANDATORY)

- **Keep It Simple**: Choose simplest metadata approach
- **Plan First**: Design metadata structure before implementation
- **Metadata Validation**: Validate all metadata changes
- **Testing**: Test with multiple tenant configurations
- **Documentation**: Document metadata schemas and APIs

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never hardcode entity structures or business logic
- ❌ Don't skip tenant isolation in metadata queries
- ❌ Never create static CRUD endpoints - use dynamic generation
- ❌ Don't ignore metadata caching for performance
- ❌ Never skip workflow permission validation
- ❌ Don't hardcode tax or billing rules - use engine metadata
- ❌ Never bypass component catalog for UI rendering
- ❌ Don't create blocking operations in workflow engine
- ❌ Never skip audit logging for metadata changes
- ❌ Don't ignore component dependency validation

## Platform-Specific Standards

- **Runtime Everything**: All business logic from metadata at runtime
- **Engine Architecture**: Separate, focused engines for each concern
- **Marketplace Ready**: Build with component sharing in mind
- **Global Scale**: Design for thousands of tenants and components
